\f0\fs24 \cf0 make a html canvas app for building modular signal flows connected by patch cables, in the style of max/msp. \
only the UI for editing, don't do any signal processing. \
every module should have the following properties: name, numAudioInputs, numControlInputs, numAudioOutputs, numControlOutputs\
make a js dictionary that defines the modules, and fill it with a few examples.\
the visual style should be minimal - rectangular black modules on white background, gray grid\
module inputs are arranged horizontally along the top of the module, outputs on the bottom. audio connections to the left, control connections to the right\
\
GUI:\
on the left hand side, an array of available chips in a vertical list. \
on the right, an empty pcb area where modules can be placed\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 module sizes and positions snap to a grid\
connections should only go vertically and horizontally, with rounded corners when changing direction\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 interactions should be keyboard only, no mouse control. \
editing is done in a hierarchy. Enter key moves down one level, Esc moves up one level.\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 arrow keys are used for edits/movements at the current level.\
D deletes the current module or connection\
\
\pard\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 The levels are:\
1. select module. arrows make selection move to the nearest module in the arrow's direction\
2. move selected module. if the module is in the left-hand list, an instance is moved to the patching area. arrow keys move the module along the grid\
3. edit module. arrow keys step through the input and output nodes, selecting current connections one by one. If a connection is selected, D deletes it. If an output node is selected, N creates a new connection from there. Then, arrow keys select the receiving module\
}